    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2ae7e2f1-1baa-5e6a-ac1d-dad75c3fb22e",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{2}$ on $A?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{1}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{2}$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{1}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{2} \\\\ & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
