      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1}$ on $A?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1}$ means that we need to multiply the first row of the matrix by $\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the first row by $\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\ & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (6) & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-6) & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (0) \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
